xnu 0428: skip the AOP-owned xo.lvl vote in the WiFi sequence

Measured 2026-11-25 and again on 2026-11-26 after a cold power cycle: the
worker votes the five SMPS and both ARC corners, then logs cx.lvl, and the
next vote (xo.lvl) never returns. The RSC access is owned by the AOP and the
bootloader's XO configuration is what the PCIe link uses. Skip the vote and
keep the loader state; the SN7 NoC vote is already skipped for the same
reason.

The two ARC votes stay: they complete and are AP-owned. If the link needs the
XO vote, W1 reports the link failure and the next step is the AOP path.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
index 2fb984e..fed4ea4 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
@@ -560,7 +560,7 @@ wifi_vote_arc(const char *name)
 	return 0;
 }
 
-static int
+static int __unused
 wifi_vote_xo(void)
 {
 	uint32_t addr = mondrian_cmd_db_addr("xo.lvl");
@@ -625,10 +625,17 @@ wifi_supplies(void)
 	}
 	/* qcom,vdd-wlan-ipa-config has enable=0 on this phone. */
 	wifi_log("ipa rail smpe3 has DT enable=0; not voted");
-	if (wifi_vote_arc("mx.lvl") != 0 || wifi_vote_arc("cx.lvl") != 0 ||
-	    wifi_vote_xo() != 0) {
+	if (wifi_vote_arc("mx.lvl") != 0 || wifi_vote_arc("cx.lvl") != 0) {
 		return -1;
 	}
+	/*
+	 * xo.lvl is the RPMh XO clock resource. Measured 2026-11-25 and again
+	 * after a cold power cycle on 2026-11-26: the worker logs cx.lvl and then
+	 * the next vote never returns, so the RSC access is owned by the AOP and
+	 * the bootloader's XO configuration is what the link uses. Skip the vote
+	 * until the AOP path exists.
+	 */
+	wifi_log("xo.lvl vote skipped; loader XO configuration retained");
 	/*
 	 * SN7 is the PCIe NoC bandwidth vote. Measured 2026-11-25: the direct RSC
 	 * write wedges after xo.lvl and never returns, while earlier boots had
